The electronic configuration of $\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$ ion is $\begin{aligned}$&amp;$\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}-\sigma$1 s^{2}, $\sigma^{*}$1 s^{2}, $\sigma$2 s^{2}, \dot{\sigma} 2 s^{2}, $\sigma$2 p_z^{2}, $\sigma$2 p_x^{2}, \\
&amp;$\pi$2 p_y^{2}, $\pi$2 p_x^{2}, $\pi$2 p_y^{2}
\end{aligned} Hence, number of antibonding electron pairs in $\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$ molecular ion are four.
